# Spectra — Controls

Spectra is played on the keyboard alone. This file defines every action the game
answers to, the keys bound to it, and which screen reads which. What the ship does
when it moves and fires is in `specs/ship.md`, and the screens the menu actions move
between are in `specs/ui.md`.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
## How input reaches the game

This game stands on no engine, so the keyboard belongs to the runtime layer you
write. It listens to the page and reports which keys are down, by their
`KeyboardEvent.code` values, along with the press edge of each. Every key below is
named by its `code`, so a binding is a physical key rather than a layout-dependent
character.
{{else}}
## How input reaches the game

Input reaches the game as named actions from the {{engine.name}} engine, which
documents them in the `engine/` directory at the root of this repository. The game
registers the layout `LAYOUT` (`dpad-4-two-buttons`), which carries four-way
movement and two buttons, and registers every action in `ACTIONS` against the keys
`BINDINGS` gives it. `BINDINGS` names each key by its `KeyboardEvent.code`, so a
binding is a physical key rather than a layout-dependent character.

The whole of `ACTIONS` is registered, so both buttons of the layout fire, and
`discharge` is registered beyond the layout.
{{/if}}

## The actions

| Action | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| `left` | Moves the ship left. |
| `right` | Moves the ship right. |
| `up` | Moves a menu highlight up. |
| `down` | Moves a menu highlight down. |
| `a` | Fires. |
| `b` | Flips the ship's band. |
| `discharge` | Releases a discharge. |
| `confirm` | Takes the highlighted menu item. |
| `back` | Leaves the current screen. |
| `pause` | Pauses live play, and resumes it from the paused screen. |
| `mute` | Toggles sound, from any screen. |

`left`, `right`, and `a` are read as holds: the ship travels while a direction is
held, and a held `a` fires every `FIRE_INTERVAL` for as long as the cooldown, the
cap, and the lockout allow a shot, as `specs/ship.md` states. `up`, `down`, `b`,
`discharge`, `confirm`, `back`, `pause`, and `mute` are read as press edges, once
per press: holding one of them acts exactly once.

## The bindings

| Action | Keys |
| --- | --- |
| `left` | `ArrowLeft`, `KeyA` |
| `right` | `ArrowRight`, `KeyD` |
| `up` | `ArrowUp`, `KeyW` |
| `down` | `ArrowDown`, `KeyS` |
| `a` | `Space`, `ArrowUp`, `KeyW` |
| `b` | `KeyF`, `ShiftLeft`, `ShiftRight` |
| `discharge` | `KeyX` |
| `confirm` | `Enter`, `Space` |
| `back` | `Escape` |
| `pause` | `Escape`, `KeyP` |
| `mute` | `KeyM` |

Several keys drive more than one action. `Space` drives `a` and `confirm`,
`ArrowUp` and `KeyW` drive `a` and `up`, and `Escape` drives `back` and `pause`. The
screen decides which one applies, by the table below, so no key ever does two things
at once.

## What each screen reads

| Screen | Reads |
| --- | --- |
| `title` | `up`, `down`, `confirm`, `mute` |
| `howto` | `back`, `mute` |
| `stageIntro` | `mute` |
| `inWave` | `left`, `right`, `a`, `b`, `discharge`, `pause`, `mute` |
| `paused` | `up`, `down`, `confirm`, `back`, `pause`, `mute` |
| `stageCleared` | `mute` |
| `gameOver` | `up`, `down`, `confirm`, `mute` |

`pause` on the `inWave` screen opens the paused screen; `pause` and `back` on the
paused screen both return to the live wave, with the wave exactly as it was.

## Menus

Every menu is vertical and is driven by `up`, `down`, and `confirm`. `up` and `down`
move the highlight by one item and wrap at both ends, so moving down from the last
item highlights the first and moving up from the first highlights the last.
`confirm` takes the highlighted item. `specs/ui.md` states each screen's items and
where each one leads.

## The debug overlay

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
The read-only debug overlay `specs/instrumentation.md` describes is shown and hidden
by the backtick key, `KeyboardEvent.code` `Backquote`. It is off when the game
starts, and it works on every screen. The overlay and its toggle are part of the
runtime layer you write, and they are not one of Spectra's actions.
{{else}}
The read-only debug overlay is the engine's, shown and hidden by the backtick key,
`KeyboardEvent.code` `Backquote` (`OVERLAY_KEY`), and off when the game starts. It
is not one of Spectra's actions. What it shows is in `specs/instrumentation.md`.
{{/if}}
